The first statement explicitly checks for `ENOSYS` and immediately jumps to fallback logic, preventing the incorrect propagation of the error. The second statement initializes `mount_id` and `mount_id_parent` to `-1`, ensuring that they have valid values before any comparisons are made. This prevents undefined behavior when comparing the mount IDs, as both will be initialized even if one of the `name_to_handle_at` calls fails.


